    given-names: Edward
date-released: "2026-06-20"
version: "0.2.4"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ETEllis/bidi-coherence-delta-calculus"
abstract: >-
  BiDi Coherence-Delta Calculus is a compact formal substrate and native
  toolchain for hybrid systems with continuous flow, guarded balanced-ternary
  commits, delayed angular coupling, nested reference frames, replayable
  durable closure, and executable coherence witnesses. Version 0.2.4 now
  includes the canonical Grammar-1 frontend, ABI 1.4, fused native execution,
  crash-safe cdc_store, typed receipts, deterministic build/install/x
  lifecycle, bridge and reducer runtimes, finite Lean/Rocq mirrors, and the
  explicitly classical RFTC six-form local control-plane experiment.
